One thing I notice is you are wearing "old gloves".  This means
you have not used a scroll of identify on them.  And that
suggests that you have not used ?ID on most of the other types
of armor in your stash.  Do that, as in identify by type.  There are
better types of armor and they may be in your stash already.  But
do note what types you do know and what types you don't know.
Once you know that "riding gloves" or whatever are "leather
gloves" there's no need to burn a scroll to discover that this
particular pair is "blessed +0 leather gloves" compared to finding
out what "fencing gloves" or "riding boots" are.

> my weapons are magicbane, trollbane and stormbringer, all granted to
> me by Anhur.  It seems to take about 4 hits to kill most things now, 2
> hits sometimes, is that good enough to keep on going down?

Trollbane is junk.  Stash it.  Magicbane and Stormbringer are
two of the best weapons in the game but for extremely different
reasons.  Wield one as your primary weapon, the other as your
secondary weapon, use "x" to swap back and forth.

But what I don't see is missiles.  You aren't throwing weapons.
Especially for a wizard, remote combat is to be used as monsters
advance and to thin crowds before they arrive.  Zap wands, cast
spells, throw missile weapons.  Even the strongest monster is
less of a problem it if is so damaged but the remote onslaught
that it dies with the first swing of Stormy.  And any monster that
doesn't survive the remote onslaught has no chance of killing
you face to face.

